MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Blink doorbell feels like a useful next addition because it connects my recent Alexa purchases with my earlier interest in door and window security.",
    "The flash drive and power strip fit my practical accessory shopping: portable file transfers complement my storage devices, and extra outlets could support my peripherals and Alexa devices. I would still check USB-C compatibility before choosing the drive."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The older Show 5 and Dot offer little reason to buy again after my second-generation Show 5 and fourth-generation Dot. The larger Show 8 interests me, but my recent display purchase makes it less timely.",
    "The AirPods Pro tips and Sony camera eyecup require specific devices I have not shown that I own. A laptop stand also lacks a clear current purpose, even though I buy keyboards and mice."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in Alexa devices seems to be treated as a reason to buy more of the same, even when an older device would duplicate something I recently bought.",
    "My frequent accessory purchases seem to imply that almost any electronics accessory will suit me, but I choose accessories for particular devices and practical needs."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent Show 5 and matching stand suggest that I have just addressed that need; an addition with a new purpose is more appealing than another similar display.",
    "Compatibility and an immediate use matter: the USB-C drive and cables need a device check, while model-specific ear tips and camera parts need evidence that I own the matching equipment."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in Alexa and practical electronics, but miss the difference between a useful addition, a recent purchase duplicated, and an accessory for a device I may not own."
}
